TickerNet was forked from TickerQ commit
3acd0f314a351817a3159d7d29a3798c8612a263 (5 July 2026). That commit is the
last commit on TickerQ's main branch distributed under the MIT License or the
Apache License 2.0. It is four commits after the TickerQ 10.4.0 package, which
was built from commit c6ed1e7daa90ab3f4c65b40319a153126a910093. TickerQ's git
history up to that commit is kept in this repository so every original change
keeps its author.

TickerQ versions from 10.5.0 onward, and its main branch from commit
13a9b544 (19 October 2026), are distributed by Arcenox LLC under a commercial
license. No code, tests, documentation or other material from those versions
is included in TickerNet. CONTRIBUTING.md explains how contributors keep it
that way.

The MongoDB persistence provider (src/TickerNet.MongoDB) was contributed to
TickerQ by Alex Brown before the fork.

TickerNet.Hub and TickerNet.Worker (src/TickerNet.Hub, src/TickerNet.Worker)
are based on the worker stream in TickerQ's remote executor and .NET SDK as
they were at the fork point (hub/ in commit 3acd0f31). They connect workers
straight to a TickerNet scheduler and do not use or connect to TickerQ Hub.

